    "updated_at": "2025-11-25T21:21:09Z",
    "body": "> In WebKit it seems that we pass this policy directly to the HTML parser and not store it on document. I suspect that forwarding ends up doing the right thing however.\n\nIn Chromium, this bit is [stored](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/parser/html_tree_builder.cc;l=303;drc=b32663066c4707a90f117b579f1993c7b74a0ad1) in the tree builder, and used for templates (without consulting the template document or copying bits into it). I suspect the same as @annevk - forwarding also probably does the right thing.",
